---

23. Email Preferences

Users should eventually be able to configure:

- Email enabled/disabled
- Frequency
- Minimum relevance threshold
- Preferred job categories
- Maximum number of jobs per email

---

24. Saved Jobs

Users should be able to save interesting jobs.

Possible states:

SAVED
APPLYING
APPLIED
REJECTED
INTERVIEW
OFFER

This allows CareerScout to eventually become more than a discovery engine and provide lightweight application tracking.

---

25. Application Tracking

The initial system should not automatically submit applications.

Instead, the system should provide:

- Original application link
- Application checklist
- Relevant resume/profile information
- User-controlled application status

The user remains responsible for deciding whether and how to apply.

